# foss-mcp build context exclusions (TC-127 / REQ-G2-047).
#
# Without this file, `docker build .` sends the ENTIRE working tree to the
# daemon as build context, including .git history, every gatectl worktree,
# and the local virtualenv - none of which any image build ever needs.
# Both Dockerfile.serving and Dockerfile.ingestion COPY only a small, explicit
# set of paths (requirements.lock, src/, config/, infra/*.py, and a handful of
# named files under tests/fixtures/<pilot>/), so nothing below removes
# anything either Dockerfile actually references.

# Version control
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.githooks/

# Governance / supervisor-worker tooling - never needed inside a built image
evidence/
ops/
plans/
project/
docs/
.gatectl-worktrees/
.kilo/
.claude/

# Local Python environment and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.benchmarks/

# Test fixture bundles (large, offline-test-only; never COPYed by a Dockerfile)
tests/fixtures/bundles

# Misc editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
